<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">BBC</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as British Broadcasting Corporation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The BBC, the British Broadcasting Corporation, is the United Kingdom's public broadcaster, founded as a company in 1922 and established by royal charter in 1927. Funded mainly by a licence fee, it became a model of public-service broadcasting. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> its broadcasts to occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a>'s appeal of 18 June 1940, made it a voice of resistance.</p></div>
